From: deepak1556 <hop2deep@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:36:06 +0900
Subject: inspector: defer remaining JS execution from V8 interrupts

Inspector messages for a main thread connection are dispatched from a
V8 interrupt handler. Queue these messages and deliver them from
microtasks. Keep later messages queued until the backlog is drained to
preserve protocol ordering. Message queuing logic is ported from
https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/4f844f4380a143d0c24b39d1df34b187b06619ae
to be aligned with upstream.

Starting the inspector I/O thread and toggling network tracking can also
call into JS from an interrupt.

Upstreamed at https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/65397.

